# Elm compilation output + sidecar fingerprints. The compiled kernel
# JS is generated by `scripts/build-elm.sh` against this tree's
# tracked Elm sources. The `.sha256` sidecars are emitted alongside
# so the build orchestrator can verify the produced JS byte-for-byte
# before staging it into the dogfood artifact.
#
# Mirrors apps/vscode/elm/completion-authority/.gitignore so the
# VSIX discovery / `.vscodeignore` / `.gitignore` interaction is
# identical across both kernels.
vendor/*.js
vendor/*.js.sha256
elm-stuff/
.elm-home/
# Allow tracked Elm binary + sidecar fingerprint in vendor/. The
# kernel JS output is gitignored; the Elm compiler is tracked so
# the build is hermetic (per completion-authority convention).
!vendor/elm
!vendor/elm.sha256
